{% comment %}
  Step 5 of 5 — final review before booking. Shows a read-only summary of
  everything collected in the previous steps (doctor, patient, mode,
  day/time) and a payment-method choice.

  MOBILE REDESIGN per a later Figma pass (node 438:7468), same instruction
  as the previous four steps: stay with the design, ignore backend
  integration.
  - Header swapped to the shared kal-booking-flow-step-header.liquid
    snippet. Since this is the last step, its step-progress-bar shows a
    plain "Final step" instead of "Next : ..." — see that snippet's own
    comment for the step_number == step_total branch that does this.
  - Heading changed from "Confirm your slot" to "Confirm booking" to
    match the export; subtext unchanged.
  - The old .kal-doctor-summary avatar row above the details card is
    gone — the export has no separate doctor-summary card on this step,
    just the details list below, now starting with its own "Doctor" row
    (previously the doctor's name only appeared in that removed summary
    row, not in the details list itself).
  - Details list gained a "Doctor" row (first) and renamed "Patient Name"
    to "Patient" to match the export; "Fee" is gone from this list
    entirely — replaced by the new Payment Method section below (two
    cards: "Pay now" at a 10%-off price, "Pay at clinic" at full price).
    Both are static mock prices (₹450 / ₹495), same category as the
    doctor's photo/fee being placeholders elsewhere in this flow.
  - Payment Method cards are click-to-select (data-kal-payment-method,
    handled by setPaymentMethod() in kal-booking-flow.js) purely for
    visual state — no amount is actually charged differently, this is a
    mockup. "Pay now" starts selected, matching the export.
  - The old "pay at the clinic" notice banner is gone — payment method is
    now an explicit choice via the cards above, not a fixed notice.
  - Button text changed from "Confirm Booking" to "Confirm payment" to
    match the export; still carries data-kal-confirm-booking and
    data-kal-goto="booking-confirmed" exactly as before — see below for
    why those remain a to-do, not wired to the backend.

  "Confirm payment" is NOT wired to the backend (explicit instruction
  throughout this build — "dont integrate it"). data-kal-confirm-booking is
  a hook with no click handler yet; when backend integration happens, this
  is where the two-call sequence documented in
  kal-booking-flow-step-patient-details.liquid (create hold, then POST
  /api/public/appointments) should fire. It also carries
  data-kal-goto="booking-confirmed" so the button navigates to the
  post-booking success screen for demo purposes in the meantime — once a
  real click handler is added for the API calls, that handler should only
  call goToStep('booking-confirmed') after a successful booking, not
  unconditionally like the plain data-kal-goto does today.

  Single shared markup, not a __mobile + __desktop split — this step was
  already fully consolidated into the shared step shell before this pass
  (see "SHARED STEP SHELL" in kal-booking-flow.css), unlike the earlier
  steps in this redesign series that still have a separate desktop
  .kal-step-entry__info block to leave untouched. There's no such
  separate desktop content here to preserve, so — unlike those steps —
  this content change (dropping the doctor-summary row and the pay
  notice, adding the Doctor row and the Payment Method cards) affects
  both breakpoints, not mobile only. The now-dead desktop-only CSS
  overrides this left behind (the doctor-summary-card margin, the
  pay-notice display:none) are addressed in kal-booking-flow.css's own
  comment.

  DESKTOP REDESIGN: same left column + full-width footer as the previous
  four steps now (see kal-booking-flow.css's .kal-step-shell--progress-panel
  section and kal-booking-flow-step-progress.liquid), current_step: 5 —
  every earlier step shows completed, "Review & payment" current (the
  last step, so there's no "Up next" row after it). This DOES replace
  the left column's content on mobile too, unlike the other four steps —
  see the note above on why this step has no separate desktop-only
  content to leave untouched; .kal-step-shell__info itself still stays
  display:none below 750px regardless (SHARED STEP SHELL), so nothing
  changes on mobile in practice.
{% endcomment %}

<div class="kal-step-confirmation kal-step-shell kal-step-shell--progress-panel">

  <div class="kal-step-entry__info kal-step-shell__info kal-concern-select__info">
    <div class="kal-concern-select__info-scroll">
      <div class="kal-concern-select__info-header">
        <h2 class="kal-step-entry__heading kal-concern-select__heading">Consultation Booking</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="kal-concern-select__info-section">
        <p class="kal-concern-select__info-label">Selected Clinic</p>
        {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-facility-picker', step_number: 5, location_text: 'Indiranagar', extra_class: 'kal-concern-select__info-pill' -%}
      </div>

      {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-step-progress', current_step: 5 -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="kal-step-shell__panel">

    {%- render 'kal-booking-flow-step-header', back_target: 'patient-details', step_number: 5, step_total: 5 -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Heading + appointment card moved BACK inside .kal-step-shell__scroll
      (reverting the earlier "only Payment Method scrolls" restructuring)
      per explicit instruction — on Step 5 of 5 specifically, only the
      progress bar stays fixed; the heading and everything below it
      (appointment card, Payment Method) scroll together, unlike every
      other step in this flow.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="kal-step-shell__scroll">
      {%- comment -%}
        Unified to one heading for both modes — "Review your appointment
        details" (previously Video Consult-only per node 625:8818) now
        replaces the older "Confirm booking" copy the In-Clinic path had
        kept, per explicit instruction to make Step 5 of 5 read the same
        across every flow/mode/width instead of a per-mode split.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="kal-step-doctor-select__intro">
        <h2 class="kal-step-doctor-select__heading">Review your appointment details</h2>
        <p class="kal-step-doctor-select__subtext">Check the details before we hold it for you.</p>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Now shown for BOTH modes — this bordered card combining the
        doctor photo/name (top, same gradient/eyebrow treatment as the
        shared .kal-appointment-card elsewhere) with Mode/Date & Time/
        Patient rows below it was Video Consult only (node 625:8818);
        In-Clinic used a separate plain "Consultation Details" list with
        its own "Doctor" row (node 438:7468). Per explicit instruction,
        In-Clinic now gets this exact same card too, so that plain list
        is gone — the doctor's identity already reads from the card's own
        photo/name header, so there's no separate "Doctor" row here.
        Mode/Date & Time/Patient reuse the exact same
        data-kal-confirm-mode/-datetime/-name hooks the old list used, so
        renderConfirmationSummary() in kal-booking-flow.js populates these
        for free with zero JS changes.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Photo temporarily removed per explicit instruction — the
        .kal-appointment-card__photo wrapper stays (so the header row's
        layout/sizing is unaffected) but renders as a plain placeholder
        box (background color only, no <img>) instead of the doctor's
        photo for now.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="kal-confirmation-appointment-card">
        <div class="kal-appointment-card kal-confirmation-appointment-card__top">
          <span class="kal-appointment-card__photo kal-appointment-card__photo--placeholder" data-kal-doctor-photo-display></span>
          <span class="kal-appointment-card__body">
            <span class="kal-appointment-card__eyebrow">Your Consultation</span>
            <span class="kal-appointment-card__name" data-kal-doctor-name-display>Dr. Neethu Jayachandran</span>
          </span>
        </div>
        <div class="kal-confirmation-appointment-card__rows">
          <div class="kal-confirmation-details__row">
            <span class="kal-confirmation-appointment-card__key">
              <span data-kal-mode-online-only hidden>{%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'mode-online' -%}</span>
              <span data-kal-mode-offline-only>{%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'location-pin' -%}</span>
              Mode
            </span>
            <span class="kal-confirmation-details__value" data-kal-confirm-mode>—</span>
          </div>
          <div class="kal-confirmation-details__row">
            <span class="kal-confirmation-appointment-card__key">
              {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'calendar-days' -%}
              Date &amp; Time
            </span>
            <span class="kal-confirmation-details__value" data-kal-confirm-datetime>—</span>
          </div>
          <div class="kal-confirmation-details__row">
            <span class="kal-confirmation-appointment-card__key">
              {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'user' -%}
              Patient
            </span>
            <span class="kal-confirmation-details__value" data-kal-confirm-name>—</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      {%- comment -%}
        Payment Method — two horizontal-row cards (node/export "Fieldset"),
        replacing this pass's earlier design of a floating "Save 10%"
        badge + centered icon/title/divider/price stack. Click-to-select
        is purely visual (setPaymentMethod() in kal-booking-flow.js just
        toggles kal-payment-option--selected) — both prices are static
        mockup values, nothing is actually charged differently. "Pay now"
        starts selected, matching the export.

        Now shown for BOTH modes — Video Consult previously got a
        separate single non-selectable "Consultation Fee" info card
        instead (no "pay at clinic" option, since the visit itself is
        online), but this pass's export for the online Confirmation
        screen (node 625:8818) shows this exact same two-card selector,
        Mode row above already saying "Video consult" — so that fee-card
        variant is gone, not just hidden, and data-kal-mode-*-only no
        longer applies to this section at all.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        kal-payment-option__badge/__divider are MOBILE ONLY (hidden at
        750px+, see CSS) — the original vertical card design's floating
        "Save 10%" pill and title/price divider line, restored after an
        earlier pass accidentally dropped them everywhere while building
        the new desktop-only horizontal row layout. Desktop instead shows
        __subtitle/__price-strike (hidden below 750px), which the
        original mobile design never had.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <div class="kal-payment-section">
        <p class="kal-payment-section__label">Payment Method</p>
        <div class="kal-payment-options">
          <button type="button" class="kal-payment-option kal-payment-option--selected" data-kal-payment-method="pay-now">
            <span class="kal-payment-option__badge">Save 10%</span>
            <span class="kal-payment-option__left">
              <span class="kal-payment-option__icon">
                {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'payment-card' -%}
              </span>
              <span class="kal-payment-option__text">
                <span class="kal-payment-option__title">Pay now</span>
                <span class="kal-payment-option__subtitle">UPI, card or netbanking</span>
              </span>
            </span>
            <span class="kal-payment-option__divider" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="kal-payment-option__price-group">
              <span class="kal-payment-option__price">&#8377;450</span>
              <span class="kal-payment-option__price-strike">&#8377;495</span>
            </span>
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="kal-payment-option" data-kal-payment-method="pay-at-clinic">
            <span class="kal-payment-option__left">
              <span class="kal-payment-option__icon kal-payment-option__icon--tint">
                {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'clinic-building' -%}
              </span>
              <span class="kal-payment-option__text">
                <span class="kal-payment-option__title">Pay at clinic</span>
                <span class="kal-payment-option__subtitle">Pay at the front desk</span>
              </span>
            </span>
            <span class="kal-payment-option__divider" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <span class="kal-payment-option__price-group">
              <span class="kal-payment-option__price">&#8377;495</span>
            </span>
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="kal-step-shell__footer kal-concern-select__footer kal-concern-select__footer--mobile">
      {%- comment -%}
        Button copy differs by mode too (node 625:8818: "Pay ₹450", vs
        In-Clinic's "Confirm payment") — one button, two text spans
        toggled the same way, so data-kal-confirm-booking/data-kal-goto
        stay on a single element regardless of mode.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__continue" data-kal-confirm-booking data-kal-goto="booking-confirmed">
        <span data-kal-mode-offline-only>Confirm payment</span>
        <span data-kal-mode-online-only hidden>Pay &#8377;450</span>
      </button>
    </div>

  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Desktop-only full-width footer bar, same pattern as the previous
    four steps — help text + Back (to Patient Details)/Continue split
    across the shared 300px/1fr grid columns. Continue keeps the exact
    same data-kal-confirm-booking/data-kal-goto hooks and mode-toggled
    copy as the mobile instance (see the button's own comment above).
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="kal-step-shell__footer kal-concern-select__footer kal-concern-select__footer--desktop">
    <div class="kal-concern-select__footer-help kal-step-entry__help">
      <span class="kal-icon kal-icon--help">
        {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'help-circle' -%}
      </span>
      <span class="kal-step-entry__help-text">Need assistance? Call us at +91 804012 3456</span>
    </div>
    <div class="kal-concern-select__footer-actions">
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__back kal-concern-select__footer-back" data-kal-back="patient-details" aria-label="Back">
        {%- render 'kal-booking-icons', icon_name: 'chevron-left' -%}
        <span>Back</span>
      </button>
      <button type="button" class="kal-step-doctor-select__continue" data-kal-confirm-booking data-kal-goto="booking-confirmed">
        <span data-kal-mode-offline-only>Confirm payment</span>
        <span data-kal-mode-online-only hidden>Pay &#8377;450</span>
      </button>
    </div>
  </div>

</div>
